From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:32:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Step past host mappings in a free-area search on
 macOS.

try_map_free_area() tries every alignment step of a range that Wine's
views leave free, a fixed mmap each. On macOS the host maps memory Wine
does not track: system libraries, Metal's memory and guard regions, one
of them 385 GB (0xfc0000000-0x7000000000) in Age of Empires II:
Definitive Edition's process. Each thread stack, placed bottom-up from
4 GB, failed through that region 64 KB at a time: the game's 175
free-area searches took 13.9 s.

After a fixed mapping fails with EEXIST, ask mach_vm_region() for the
mapping in the way and continue past it. The game's 195 searches now
take 22 ms in all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 62d6bea..a4f17be 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1562,6 +1562,34 @@ static void* try_map_free_area( void *base, void *end, ptrdiff_t step,
             (step < 0 && (char *)start - (char *)base < -step) ||
             step == 0)
             break;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        {
+            /* Wine's views don't cover what the host mapped on its own (system libraries, Metal's memory, the
+             * system's guard regions, one of them hundreds of GB): step past the host mapping in the way at once
+             * instead of trying every granularity step inside it, a failed system call each. */
+            mach_vm_address_t addr = (mach_vm_address_t)start;
+            mach_vm_size_t region_size = 0;
+            vm_region_basic_info_data_64_t info;
+            mach_msg_type_number_t count = VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_COUNT_64;
+            mach_port_t object;
+
+            if (!mach_vm_region( mach_task_self(), &addr, &region_size, VM_REGION_BASIC_INFO_64,
+                                 (vm_region_info_t)&info, &count, &object ) &&
+                addr < (mach_vm_address_t)start + size)
+            {
+                if (step > 0)
+                {
+                    char *next = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)addr + region_size + step - 1, step - 1 );
+                    if (next > (char *)start) { start = next; continue; }
+                }
+                else if ((char *)addr >= (char *)base + size)
+                {
+                    char *next = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)addr - size, -step - 1 );
+                    if (next < (char *)start) { start = next; continue; }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+#endif
         start = (char *)start + step;
     }
 
